WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actress.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.669
You know her from her work
on shows like

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.238
"Parks and Recreation"
and "Legion"

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.339
and films like
"Happiest Season."

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:10.910
Her children's book, "The Legend
of the Christmas Witch"

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.645
is available today.
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.847
our very good friend
Aubrey Plaza, everyone.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.582
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:26.592 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:36.602 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:41.073 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:44.844
-Aubrey.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.414
I feel like
you did something different

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.749
to your look over the pandemic.
-No.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.584
This is how I always dress,
Seth.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.153
-Are you sure?
It's not a haircut or something?

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.521
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:56.689
-This is very exciting.
First of all,

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.558
it is great to see you.
-You too, man.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.395
-And -- And now you have this
book, "The Christmas Witch."

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.796
-Yes.
-Now, I have not --

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.065
I was not familiar with witches
in the Christmastime.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.168
What -- What gave you --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.270
What gave you this idea?
It shouldn't be --

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.705
It's "The Legend
of the Christmas Witch."

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.642
-This is "The Legend
of the Christmas Witch."

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.310
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.279
She's always existed, Seth.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.248
And just now,
we finally get her story.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.150
-Oh!
-Yes.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.218
-Have you always been drawn
to Halloween as a holiday?

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:29.355
-Yes. Halloween has always been
kind of my thing.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.823
-Uh-huh.
-And through the past

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.592
couple years, I've been doing
this performance kind of art,

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.928
witchy thing on Halloween,
where I scare all the kids

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.031
in the neighborhood.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.666
I don't have children,
so it's extra weird.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:43.436
[ Laughter ]
And I --

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.838
Yeah, I dress up like a witch,
and I do this thing with them,

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.008
where I, like, throw candy
at them, which they like,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.543
but then I also
try to scare them

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.446
and freak them out,
which they don't like.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.481
But it really gets them
all riled up.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.350
[ Laughter ]
And they come back for more.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.352
They can't get enough.
And I -- I throw it

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:03.289
and scream like,
"I don't want to be doing this!"

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.991
And they're like,
"You don't have to!"

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:08.061
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Yes, I do!"

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.830
And it goes back and forth
like that all night long.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.399
And -- yeah.
-Do you feel like you intimidate

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.401
the other neighbors,
in that they feel like

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.304
they're not putting the same
energy into the -- the spirit?

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.774
-I mean, Hank and Linda...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.009
...you got to up your game.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.210
-And you sort of do it
from your front steps?

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.311
Is that where you --
-Yeah.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.815
I create a whole kind of
graveyard scene...

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.050
-Okay.
-...in my front yard, with --

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.385
I hide behind the tombstones.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:36.756
I actually put the bowl of candy
with a spotlight on it,

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.891
and I hide,
and so then the kids walk up,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.927
and they all know, "Okay.
There's candy in there,"

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.561
and they all discuss,
"All right, you go.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.530
You -- You put
your hand in there."

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.132
And they all are scared,
and then one brave

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.434
little kid does it,
and the minute he reaches in,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.204
I -- I attack.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.172
And they cry.
A lot of them cry.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.941
-Sure.
-It's disturbing.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.308
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.577
-And now you've made them
a children's book.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:00.045
-Yes.
-This same person.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:03.282
-[ Cackling ] Y-e-e-e-es!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.551
-So, now, where did you get
this idea of a Christmas Witch?

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.753
This is sort of --
Is it based on anything?

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.790
-First of all,
I get sad after Halloween.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.158
-Yeah.
-And I -- I had to hang up

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:15.661
my witch hat and broom,
and I -- and I always get sad.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.163
So, a couple years ago, I said,
"You know what?

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.297
I'm not gonna do that this year.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.199
I'm gonna carry it through
to Christmas."

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.367
-That's great.
-And I'm gonna -- I'm gonna

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.135
dress up like a witch
at Christmas.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.104
And instead of throwing candy,
I'm gonna throw presents

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.772
and see if I can get
the same reaction.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.440
[ Laughter ]
And I did.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.177
-Yeah, I would imagine.
-So, I -- Yeah, I kind of

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.012
developed this
Christmas Witch character

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.181
just out of boredom, really.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.583
And I just -- I tried it out
on my manager.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.619
I put a sack of presents in --
in a bag or something --

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.256
I think in a garbage bag, maybe.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.991
And I put a witch costume on,
but I gave it a Christmas flair.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.060
I think I had some bells
on my head or something.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.164
And then, I told her, "I'm gonna
come scare your son, Max.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.665
So, tell him the -- tell him
the Christmas Witch is coming.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:55.301
See how he feels about it.
Tell him he's gonna

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.969
get a present,
but it's gonna be very scary."

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.237
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.705
And Max was kind of
my guinea pig.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:02.174
And I -- And I basically just
went there, hid in the bushes,

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:05.345
and I worked out my shtick.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:08.113
-I want to point out, like,
I think sometimes kids' books

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:10.783
are, you know, there are sort of
a few words on each page,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.151
it's a little simple.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.186
-This is -- You're --
You're world-building here.

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:15.488
-I am.
-I just want to show that, like,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.424
whenever you see a map
on the first page of a book,

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.092
you know that you're --
you're getting

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:23.362
your bang for your buck in here.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.530
Yeah, that helped.
That was very helpful.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.798
-Oh, sorry.
Um, yes.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.100
So Julia Iredale
is our illustrator.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.303
She's a -- She's a -- an amazing
illustrator from Vancouver.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.172
And we -- we talked to her
about having a map,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.774
because, yes,
we are world-building.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:39.311
We're going to have
an amusement-park world,

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.414
a little section
of the amusement park,

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.949
the Christmas Witch
amusement park,

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.250
and little kids
are gonna grow up knowing,

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.119
"Oh, the Christmas Witch
is coming.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.621
And -- And we know where
she came from, the Black Forest.

00:04:49.621 --> 00:04:51.190
[ Laughter ]
And then she got in the boat

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.325
with her peng-- She has penguins
instead of reindeer."

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:54.560
-Great.
-"She's on the South Pole

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.129
instead of the North Pole."
You get the idea.

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.831
[ Laughter ]
And, um --

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.032
-I mean,
I get that there is an idea.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.601
-Anyway, it's all in the book.
-Yeah, right.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.435
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:07.973
Now, I want to finish
by remarking

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:09.875
on some exciting personal news.
-Okay.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.411
-You were one of the people
that I think --

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.879
I think it's really sweet --
during the pandemic,

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.581
during a very difficult time...
-Yeah.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.082
-...you got married.
Congratulations.

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:21.854
-Thanks.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:27.159
-Imagine --
Imagine a smaller ceremony.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:31.697
-Yes. It was just a joke
that went too far.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.699
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.402
It was our --
It was our anniversary and --

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.837
Yes, we'd been in lockdown,
as everyone was,

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:42.441
and the quarantine kind of --
and we were just like,

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.911
"You know, it's our anniversary.
We should do something special."

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.846
And I was like,
"Why don't we just get married?

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:49.515
How about that?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.884
And then, he was like,
"Well, I don't think we can.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.420
It's probably not possible to do
it on a Sunday like this."

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.222
And I was like,
"Well, I'm gonna google it."

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.190
[ Laughter ]
And I did.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:01.260
And I found a website
called 1hourmarriage.com.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.796
[ Light laughter ]
And I called the number,

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:07.333
and I said, "Can you get us
married in an hour,

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.636
like -- like you advertise?"
And they said, "I don't know.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.638
We're in Alhambra,
so how about tomorrow?"

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:18.477
And I said, "No, I want
the hour thing that you do."

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.880
And then,
silence on the other end.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.448
Then he said,
"How about two hours,

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:26.052
and it's an extra
hundred bucks or whatever."

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:29.422
And I said, "Sold."
And then, a very nice man, yeah,

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:32.324
from Alhambra, came in a
Hawaiian shirt with a briefcase.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:35.628
I, uh --
I was, you know, saging.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.163
-That's how you know it's legal,
when the brief --

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.331
when there's a briefcase.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:40.533
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.469
I created a love altar
of our love objects.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.238
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.906
And I smoked it out,
you know, in the yard.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:49.375
-Yeah.
-And then, there is a witch --

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.310
This is an entirely --
has nothing to do

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.644
with the Christmas --
-A separate witch.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.580
-There's a separate witch thing,
where there was a witch

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.282
that was living across the
street during the quarantine.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.617
Her name was Dandelion.
We became friends.

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.552
-Now, did you --
Did she have to tell you

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:01.987
she was a witch,
or did you know?

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:04.624
-Oh, she -- that's pretty much
the first thing she says

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:05.758
when you meet her...
-Yeah.

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:06.826
-...that she's
a fourth-generation witch

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.260
from Tennessee.
-Gotcha.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.662
-I kind of became
her apprentice.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.097
But anyway, she -- We --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:13.599
You know, this was, like --
the wedding was like,

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.835
"Aah! We're doing it in an hour,
two hours."

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:18.637
So, I just went over
to her place, and I said,

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:20.172
"I think we're gonna
get married in the yard.

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:22.541
If you could do a spell
or tell me if this is, like,

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:24.410
a good idea, you know..."
-Yeah.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.280
-"...cosmically, astrologically,
that would be great,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.314
or whatever you want to do..."
-I would imagine

00:07:29.314 --> 00:07:31.750
when you're an across-the-street
witch, that's your dream...

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.452
-Oh, yeah.
-...that somebody comes to you

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.454
and asks for information
like that on the fast.

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:37.923
-I mean, we were meant
to be neighbors.

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:39.958
[ Laughter ]
100%.

00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:41.260
-Had she signed off
on everything?

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.262
-Oh, yeah. She went,
"I have just the thing."

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:46.332
She went into her house,
literally cackled.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.200
[ Laughter ]
I could hear her from outside.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.670
And then brought me
this rosemary crown

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.139
that I wore in my hair
while I got married.

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.809
And, hopefully,
it's not a curse.

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.844
-Well, so far, so good, right?

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:03.048
-So far, so good, right, honey?
[ Cackling ]

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:05.217
-You guys, that's Aubrey Plaza!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:08.187
"The Legend of the Christmas
Witch" is available today!

